    <bpmn:process id="W_W698" name="W698. Safety Data Sheet (SDS) Lifecycle Management &amp; Distribution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New hazmat SKU added to assortment per W1; vendor issues SDS update (new formulation, regulatory change); annual SDS compliance review; DENR/DOLE inspection identifies SDS gap
Frequency: Continuous for new SKU intake; quarterly vendor SDS update check; annual comprehensive review
Volume: ~5,000–6,000 hazmat-classified SKUs (~15% of 35,000 active SKUs) requiring current SDS on file; ~200–400 SDS updates/year from vendors
Owner: Environmental Compliance Officer
Participants: Merchandising (new SKU intake), Procurement (vendor SDS requests), DC Safety Officer, Store Safety Officer, IT (SDS system management), Vendor
Source: workflow W698 — Safety Data Sheet (SDS) Lifecycle Management &amp; Distribution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W698_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W698_Lane1" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W698_Lane2" name="Environmental Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W698_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W698_Lane4" name="Safety Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W698_Lane5" name="Safety Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W698_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W698_Start7" name="New hazmat SKU added to assortment per W1; vendor issues SDS update (new formulation…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W698_Task8" name="SDS intake for new SKU">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: SDS intake for new SKU: when Merchandising adds a new hazmat SKU per W1: (a) Procurement requests SDS from vendor in GHS-compliant format (16-section format per Philippine DOLE DO 252-25); (b) Environmental Compliance Officer reviews SDS for completeness: all 16 sections populated, Philippine-specific emergency contacts, GHS hazard classification present; (c) if SDS is incomplete or not GHS-compliant: reject and request compliant version from vendor; (d) upload approved SDS to ERP SDS repository linked to Item Master record; (e) system flags SKU as &quot;SDS Required — Active&quot;
Responsible (R): Procurement / Environmental Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30-60 min per new SDS</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W698_Task9" name="SDS update monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SDS update monitoring: quarterly, Environmental Compliance Officer: (a) sends automated SDS currency inquiry to top 50 hazmat vendors: &quot;Please confirm current SDS on file is still valid, or provide updated SDS&quot;; (b) for vendors who do not respond within 30 days: escalate to Procurement for follow-up; (c) for vendors who provide updated SDS: review and replace in repository per step 1 process; (d) track SDS age: flag any SDS older than 4 years (approaching the 5-year internal refresh threshold — no statutory validity; currency is per formulation change) for priority vendor follow-up
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W698_Task10" name="SDS distribution to locations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: SDS distribution to locations: when new or updated SDS is added to repository: (a) system automatically pushes SDS to all 200 stores and 4 DCs where the SKU is in active assortment; (b) SDS accessible via: (i) ERP Item Master inquiry (any user can pull up SDS from SKU screen), (ii) mobile app for DC Safety Officers and Store Safety Officers, (iii) printed SDS binder in each store&#x27;s Paint/Chemical department and each DC&#x27;s Hazmat Zone; (c) Store/DC Safety Officer acknowledges receipt and updates printed binder if applicable
Responsible (R): System / Store Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Environmental Compliance Officer
Duration: Automated push + 15 min per location for printed binder update</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W698_Task11" name="SDS accessibility verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SDS accessibility verification: during quarterly workplace safety inspection per W141: (a) inspector verifies SDS binder is present, complete, and current in Paint/Chemical department and DC Hazmat Zone; (b) inspector checks 10 random hazmat SKUs on shelf vs. SDS binder: all 10 must have current SDS present; (c) any gaps: Store Safety Officer must obtain SDS within 7 days; (d) accessibility check: verify employees know how to access SDS digitally via ERP or mobile app
Responsible (R): Safety Inspector / Store Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Environmental Compliance Officer
Duration: 30 min per inspection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W698_Task12" name="SDS for spill/incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: SDS for spill/incident response: during hazmat spill response per W238: (a) first responder accesses SDS for spilled product via mobile app (offline-capable); (b) SDS provides: hazard identification, first aid measures, fire-fighting measures, accidental release measures, handling and storage, PPE requirements; (c) post-incident: verify SDS was accessible and used during response; if SDS was unavailable, add to corrective action
Responsible (R): Safety Officer
Accountable (A): Environmental Compliance Officer
Duration: During W238</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W698_Task13" name="Annual SDS compliance audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual SDS compliance audit: Environmental Compliance Officer conducts annual comprehensive review: (a) total hazmat SKUs vs. total SDS on file (target: 100% coverage); (b) SDS age distribution: % current (&lt;3 years), % aging (3-4 years), % due for refresh (4–5 years), % overdue (&gt;5 years); (c) vendor responsiveness rate for quarterly update inquiries; (d) location accessibility compliance rate from W141 inspections; (e) report to COO and VP Legal with recommendations for improvement
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W698_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W698_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W698_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W698_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-315 (ensure controlled execution — Hazmat Management (PA-24.3).) | - operational: Environmental Compliance Officer review and approval gate
Owner: Environmental Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W698_Assoc16" sourceRef="W698_Annotation15" targetRef="W698_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W698_Flow17" sourceRef="W698_Start7" targetRef="W698_Task8" />
