    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W699" name="W699. Hazmat Transportation &amp; Carrier Compliance Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Hazmat shipment dispatched from vendor to DC; hazmat inter-DC transfer; hazmat delivery to customer from store; annual carrier compliance review
Frequency: Daily for DC inbound hazmat shipments; weekly for inter-DC transfers; ad-hoc for customer hazmat deliveries; annual carrier review
Volume: ~15% of inbound shipments contain hazmat items (paint, chemicals, adhesives, batteries); ~300–500 hazmat shipments/month across 4 DCs
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: DC Safety Officer, Fleet Manager, 3PL Carrier, Procurement (vendor shipping coordination), Environmental Compliance Officer
Source: workflow W699 — Hazmat Transportation &amp; Carrier Compliance Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W699_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W699_Lane1" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W699_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W699_Lane3" name="DC Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W699_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W699_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W699_Start6" name="Hazmat shipment dispatched from vendor to DC; hazmat inter-DC transfer; hazmat delivery…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task7" name="Carrier qualification for hazmat transport">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Carrier qualification for hazmat transport: Logistics Manager maintains list of qualified hazmat carriers: (a) carrier must have DENR-registered hazmat transport permit; (b) carrier vehicles must have proper placarding (hazmat diamond labels per GHS); (c) carrier drivers must have hazmat handling training certificate; (d) carrier insurance must include hazmat spill coverage; (e) annual re-qualification: verify permits, insurance, and training currency
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2-3 days initial per carrier; 1 day/year per carrier re-qualification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task8" name="Vendor shipping instruction for hazmat">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor shipping instruction for hazmat: for Purchase Orders containing hazmat items per W2B: (a) Procurement includes hazmat shipping requirements in PO: GHS-compliant packaging, proper labeling (UN number, proper shipping name, hazard class, packing group), hazmat shipping documentation (dangerous goods declaration); (b) for imported hazmat: verify BOC hazmat import permit per W239; (c) Procurement communicates expected delivery date to DC Safety Officer for receiving preparation
Responsible (R): Procurement
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 15-30 min per PO containing hazmat</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task9" name="Hazmat shipment receiving at DC">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Hazmat shipment receiving at DC: when hazmat shipment arrives at DC: (a) DC Receiving Clerk verifies carrier qualification (hazmat transport permit current); (b) verify shipment documentation: dangerous goods declaration, bill of lading with hazmat classification; (c) visual inspection: packaging integrity, GHS labels present and legible, no leaks or damage; (d) if carrier is unqualified or documentation is missing: refuse delivery and notify Logistics Manager; (e) if packaging is damaged or leaking: contain per W238 spill response, refuse damaged items, document for vendor claim
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Clerk / DC Safety Officer
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 15-30 min per hazmat shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task10" name="Inter-DC hazmat transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inter-DC hazmat transfer: when hazmat items are transferred between DCs: (a) system auto-selects qualified hazmat carrier from approved list; (b) transfer documentation includes: hazmat manifest, GHS classification for each item, emergency contact numbers; (c) packaging verification: ensure items are properly packaged for transport (original containers or compliant repackaging); (d) receiving DC follows step 3 receiving procedures
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / DC Safety Officer
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30-60 min per inter-DC transfer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task11" name="Customer hazmat delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer hazmat delivery: for customer orders containing hazmat items delivered from store per W668: (a) system flags order as containing hazmat items; (b) verify delivery carrier is qualified for hazmat transport (Lalamove/Transportify may not accept hazmat items); (c) if no qualified carrier available: customer must pick up at store (inform customer of hazmat pickup requirement); (d) package per W237 hazmat handling requirements with GHS labels visible; (e) delivery manifest includes emergency contact numbers
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 15-20 min per hazmat delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W699_Task12" name="Annual carrier compliance audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual carrier compliance audit: Logistics Manager conducts annual review: (a) audit all hazmat carriers for permit and insurance currency; (b) review carrier incident history: spills, accidents, documentation failures during the year; (c) carrier scorecard update: on-time delivery, documentation compliance, incident rate; (d) disqualify carriers with expired permits or repeated compliance failures; (e) identify new carrier candidates for qualification per step 1
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2-3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W699_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W699_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W699_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W699_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-315 (ensure controlled execution — Hazmat Management (PA-24.3).) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W699_Assoc15" sourceRef="W699_Annotation14" targetRef="W699_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W699_Flow16" sourceRef="W699_Start6" targetRef="W699_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W699_Flow17" sourceRef="W699_Task7" targetRef="W699_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W699_Flow18" sourceRef="W699_Task8" targetRef="W699_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W699_Flow19" sourceRef="W699_Task9" targetRef="W699_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W699_Flow20" sourceRef="W699_Task10" targetRef="W699_Task11" />
