    <bpmn:process id="W_W803" name="W803. Hazmat Regulatory Change Management &amp; Compliance Update" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DENR, DOLE, FDA, or BOC issues new regulation or amendment affecting hazmat storage, handling, transportation, or disposal
Frequency: Ad-hoc; estimated 5-10 significant regulatory changes/year affecting BuildRight hazmat operations
Volume: ~5,000–6,000 hazmat SKUs across 200 stores and 4 DCs potentially affected by each regulatory change
Owner: Environmental Compliance Officer
Participants: ESG Manager, VP Legal, Merchandising, Procurement, DC Safety Officers, Store Safety Officers, Compliance Team per W657
Source: workflow W803 — Hazmat Regulatory Change Management &amp; Compliance Update</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W803_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W803_Lane1" name="Environmental Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W803_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W803_Start3" name="DENR, DOLE, FDA, or BOC issues new regulation or amendment affecting hazmat storage…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W803_Task4" name="Regulatory Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Regulatory Monitoring: Environmental Compliance Officer monitors hazmat regulatory changes: (a) DENR-EMB website and circulars for environmental compliance updates; (b) DOLE Bureau of Working Conditions for workplace safety updates; (c) FDA for household hazardous substance regulations; (d) BOC customs circulars for import classification changes; (e) integrate with W657 regulatory change management for centralized tracking; (f) subscribe to regulatory update services from Philippine law firms specializing in environmental law
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2-3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W803_Task5" name="Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact Assessment: When significant regulatory change is identified: (a) Environmental Compliance Officer reviews the regulation in detail; (b) assess impact on BuildRight operations: which hazmat SKUs are affected, which locations, which processes (storage, handling, training, transportation, disposal); (c) determine compliance deadline; (d) identify gap between current BuildRight practices and new requirements; (e) estimate cost of compliance (training, equipment, process changes); (f) prepare Impact Assessment Report for VP Legal and COO
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2-5 days per regulation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W803_Task6" name="Compliance Action Plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance Action Plan: Develop and implement compliance plan: (a) update W236 storage and segregation rules if affected; (b) update W237 training materials and schedule refresher training if training requirements changed; (c) update W698 SDS management if SDS format requirements changed; (d) update W699 transportation procedures if carrier permit requirements changed; (e) update Item Master hazmat classification per W252 if classification criteria changed; (f) update W82 disposal procedures if waste disposal regulations changed; (g) communicate changes to all 200 stores and 4 DCs with implementation timeline
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1-4 weeks per regulation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W803_Task7" name="Training &amp; Communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Training &amp; Communication: For regulatory changes requiring employee action: (a) update training materials per W655; (b) schedule and execute training for affected personnel (DC Safety Officers, Store Safety Officers, receiving staff, hazmat handlers); (c) update safety signage per new GHS or Philippine-specific labeling requirements; (d) issue Compliance Bulletin to all locations via W506 unified compliance calendar; (e) document training completion for regulatory audit readiness
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer / HR
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1-3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W803_Task8" name="Verification &amp; Audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Verification &amp; Audit: After compliance deadline: (a) Environmental Compliance Officer verifies implementation at sample locations (minimum 5 stores + 1 DC); (b) check: updated signage, completed training, updated SDS, modified storage, updated procedures; (c) Internal Audit includes new regulation in next audit cycle per W339 regulatory compliance audit; (d) if gaps found: escalate to COO for immediate corrective action
Responsible (R): Environmental Compliance Officer / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2-3 days per regulation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W803_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W803_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W803_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W803_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-315 (ensure controlled execution — Hazmat Management (PA-24.3).) | - operational: VP Legal guidance required to interpret applicability of new regulations
Owner: Environmental Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W803_Assoc11" sourceRef="W803_Annotation10" targetRef="W803_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow12" sourceRef="W803_Start3" targetRef="W803_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow13" sourceRef="W803_Task4" targetRef="W803_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow14" sourceRef="W803_Task5" targetRef="W803_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow15" sourceRef="W803_Task6" targetRef="W803_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow16" sourceRef="W803_Task7" targetRef="W803_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W803_Flow17" sourceRef="W803_Task8" targetRef="W803_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W803_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W803_plane" bpmnElement="W_W803">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W803_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W803_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W803_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W803_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
